  isFinal: 0
  edition: "Baku  \xB7  Tuesday edition  \xB7  Vol. XII, No. 201"
  flavorHeadlines:
  - Caspian Fishery Quotas Under Review Again
  - Old City Tram Line to Reopen "Next Spring", Says Ministry
  - Heatwave Expected to Break by Friday
  leadHeadline: Night Staff Flee Shuttered Diner. "Scratching" Heard From Locked
    Pantry
  leadDetail: Reported near 2 AM, Harbor Street Diner, Harbor Street.
  leadReaction:
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: Harbor Street. Walking distance. Beats staring at the ceiling.
  arrivalLines:
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: Harbor Street Diner. Shut a month, smells like a year.
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: Look around before anything looks at me. The Book's in my coat if I need
      it.
  bookRevealLines: []
  identifyLines:
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: The Famished. A cook who starved in his own kitchen and came back hungry.
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: Rock salt from the kitchen where it died. The pantry, then.
  wrongToolLine: I try the {0}. The scratching behind the door gets louder. Wrong
    tool.
  resolveLines:
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: A line of the kitchen's own rock salt across the threshold.
  - speaker: 
    text: Something behind the pantry door breathes out, long and tired, and the
      cold goes with it.
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: Eat well, chef.
